Basic Linux Commands
•	pwd: Prints the current working directory.
o	Sample usage: pwd [1]
•	ls: Lists files and folders in the current directory.
o	Sample usage: ls -la
•	cd: Changes the current directory.
o	Sample usage: cd /home/user/documents
•	mkdir: Creates a new directory.
o	Sample usage: mkdir my_folder
•	cp: Copies files or directories.
o	Sample usage: cp file.txt backup.txt
•	mv: Moves or renames files and directories.
o	Sample usage: mv old.txt new.txt
o	
•	rm: Deletes files or directories.
o	Sample usage: rm file.txt
•	cat: Displays the contents of a file.
o	Sample usage: cat notes.txt
•	grep: Searches for text inside files.
o	Sample usage: grep "error" log.txt
•	chmod: Changes file permissions.
o	Sample usage: chmod +x script.sh
